title: Niko0
---

<<gatherVars>>

When you entered the library, the smell of new books and warm coffee washed
over you. The murmurs of students studying filled the room. The library was
always cozy, a place you liked to study and read assigned books.

A good candidate for this essay would definitely be here, you thought.
Bookworms could have the best opinions on life. You looked around for the
right person to ask.

You: "This is impossible,"

You sighed. Everyone was in groups, studying or chatting. You felt too awkward
approaching a group to ask about your questionnaire.

Turning to a bookcase, you shrugged and scanned the shelves. Nothing caught
your interest, and that's when you turned your head.

To your right stood a lone man dressed in blacks and browns, like a character
from a gothic novel. The only bright features were the blonde highlights in
his hair and his amber eyes as they scanned the books.

His hands brushed the spines delicately before stopping and selecting one
with precision. He opened it one-handed and read a few pages before nodding.

Then he turned, meeting your gaze with piercing eyes.

Startled, you quickly looked away, your face warming with embarrassment. You
heard him sigh.

<<set $NikoDiaImage = true>>
Niko: "Do you need something?"
<<set $NikoDiaImage = false>>

His voice was gravelly and rough, laced with annoyance. You didn't want to
bother him, but you needed a candidate. Maybe approaching a group would have
been easier.

